  "goodToKnow": "Die Vergessenheit is oblivion, the state of being forgotten, used almost only in set phrases: in Vergessenheit geraten (to fall into oblivion), der Vergessenheit entreißen (to rescue from oblivion). Many women artists and scientists in German history geraten in Vergessenheit and are now being rediscovered. Vergessen means to forget, and vergesslich forgetful. It has no plural."
